<!-- =========================================
     SECTION 2: WHY WE STARTED [DARK-BOLD #383838 CHARCOAL GRAY]
     Columns: LEFT = Team Photo | RIGHT = Story
     ========================================= -->
<section class="sec-dark-bold">
    <div class="container-wide">
        <div class="grid-2col sec2-mobile-reverse">
            <!-- Left Column: Team Photo -->
            <div class="sec2-img-col">
                <img src="images/team.jpg" alt="Ben Wiseman and Forged Labor Crew" class="sqsp-clean-img" />
            </div>

            <!-- Right Column: Heading & Paragraphs -->
            <div class="sec2-text-col">
                <h2 style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3.8vw, 3rem); color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-transform: lowercase;">
                    why we started.
                </h2>
                
                <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.65;">
                    Too many moving companies send sluggish, careless workers who treat your home like a burden. They take smoke breaks every 15 minutes, stare at their phones, ding walls, and surprise you with hidden fees when the invoice arrives.
                </p>

                <p style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                    When you hire <strong>FORGED LABOR</strong>, you’re hiring people shaped by real-world labor, discipline, and physical excellence. We show up in shape, on time, and ready to hustle.
                </p>

                <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #e4e4e7; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.65;">
                    Ben Wiseman founded Forged Labor in Cleveland, Tennessee to redefine what a moving company should be. Like steel forged by fire, our work ethic was built through real sweat and life experience. We recruit movers who take personal pride in their stamina, politeness, and property protection.
                </p>

                <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #e4e4e7; line-height: 1.65;">
                    From the first box loaded to the final piece placed in your new home, our crew maintains focused momentum. <strong>Every single time.</strong>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================
     SECTION 3: MEET THE LEADERSHIP & OFFICE TEAM [WHITE SECTION]
     ========================================= -->
<section class="sec-white">
    <div class="container-wide">
        <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem); color: var(--brand-accent); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); letter-spacing: -0.01em;">
                FORGED LABOR
            </h2>
            <h4 style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: #000000; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 900;">
                MEET THE LEADERSHIP &amp; OFFICE TEAM
            </h4>
        </div>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 2rem;">

            <!-- 1. Ben Wiseman -->
            <article class="accordion-box" style="padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <img src="images/team-ben.jpg" alt="Ben Wiseman - Owner, Forged Labor" style="width: 96px; height: 96px; flex-shrink: 0; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; border: 2px solid #000000;" />
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.4rem; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                            BEN WISEMAN
                        </h3>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #383838; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                            Owner | Frontline Operations Manager
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accordion-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Originally from Calhoun, Tennessee, Ben attended McMinn County High School and spent much of his childhood around Athens. He’s watched the Cleveland area grow tremendously over the years, even remembering when much of Paul Huff Parkway was nothing but trees! In 2020, he officially made Cleveland home after purchasing his first house.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Before entering the moving industry, Ben worked at Walmart, O’Charley’s, and Aldi before transitioning into gig work through platforms like DoorDash, Uber Eats, and Instacart. His entrepreneurial journey began with his own small grocery delivery business, eventually leading to a conversation with his friend Bradley about finding ways to earn extra income. In July 2025, that conversation turned into what would become Forged Labor. What started as two guys looking for a side hustle quickly grew into something much bigger.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Outside of work, Ben has always been passionate about fitness, health, and human performance—ranging from strength training and nutrition to psychology, sleep science, and overall wellness. One of his long-term dreams is to open a training facility combining basketball, MMA, fitness, and mental wellness for athletes and everyday people alike. On a more personal note, he’d love to take his niece and family to Disney World!</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">For Ben, Forged Labor represents much more than moving furniture. After hearing countless stories about stressful moving experiences and unreliable companies, he saw an opportunity to do things differently: exceptional service, genuine kindness, supporting other small businesses, and making professional moving accessible to families from all walks of life.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- 2. Breanna "Bre" Wiseman -->
            <article class="accordion-box" style="padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <img src="images/team-bre.jpg" alt="Breanna &quot;Bre&quot; Wiseman - Co-Owner, Forged Labor" style="width: 96px; height: 96px; flex-shrink: 0; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; border: 2px solid #000000;" />
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.4rem; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                            BREANNA &ldquo;BRE&rdquo; WISEMAN
                        </h3>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #383838; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                            Co-Owner | Human Resources &amp; Creative Director
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accordion-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Originally from Niota, Tennessee, Bre moved to Cleveland to pursue her education, although her academic journey eventually took her in a different direction than she’d originally planned. She and her husband, Ben, married in 2023 and have shared a dream of building a business together ever since.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">With two degrees in psychology and plans to complete her master’s degree in 2027, Bre has a strong passion for understanding people, supporting mental health, and making a positive difference in the lives of others.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Outside of work, she loves spending quality time with her friends, family, and pets. She and Ben also share a long-term dream of opening a comprehensive fitness and wellness facility that combines physical transformation with mental health services.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">At Forged Labor, Bre brings compassion, creativity, and a genuine commitment to taking care of people. Whether she’s supporting the crew behind the scenes, making sure everyone is fed and hydrated, helping with jobs, or going the extra mile for customers, she believes the little things make a big difference—creating a workplace where people feel valued and extending that same care to every customer.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- 3. Dez Caudill -->
            <article class="accordion-box" style="padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <img src="images/team-dez.jpg" alt="Dez Caudill - Office Manager, Forged Labor" style="width: 96px; height: 96px; flex-shrink: 0; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; border: 2px solid #000000;" />
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.4rem; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                            DEZ CAUDILL
                        </h3>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #383838; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                            Office Manager
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accordion-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Originally from London, Kentucky, Dez spent her middle and high school years in Athens, Tennessee, before returning to Kentucky for eight years. When she eventually made her way back to Tennessee, she initially settled in Knoxville before moving to Cleveland to be closer to her friends and support system.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Dez and Bre have actually been friends since the summer before middle school! When Bre mentioned that Forged Labor was growing and needed additional support, the opportunity felt like a natural fit. Dez was excited to join a smaller, close-knit company where she could contribute to something meaningful while building a new chapter of her own life.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Outside of the office, Dez enjoys cooking, creating art, listening to music, playing guitar, and spending time outdoors. She’s also a proud mom to her eight-year-old son and a tuxedo cat named Hercules!</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">As Office Manager, Dez helps ensure customers receive the communication, organization, and personal attention they deserve. She takes pride in being part of a company that values honesty, empathy, reliability, and genuine human connection—hoping to make every customer’s moving experience a little easier and a lot more positive.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- 4. Bruno Wigglebutt Wiseman -->
            <article class="accordion-box" style="padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <img src="images/team-bruno.jpg" alt="Bruno Wigglebutt Wiseman - Chief Morale Officer, Forged Labor" style="width: 96px; height: 96px; flex-shrink: 0; object-fit: cover; object-position: center center; border: 2px solid #000000;" />
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.4rem; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                            BRUNO WIGGLEBUTT WISEMAN
                        </h3>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #383838; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                            Chief Morale Officer | Head of Security | Professional Treat Inspector
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accordion-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Originally from Niota, Tennessee, Bruno joined the Wiseman family in July 2024 after being adopted and leaving his days of homelessness behind. Since then, he’s worked his way up the corporate ladder to become one of Forged Labor’s most beloved (and arguably most demanding) employees.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Bruno’s qualifications include expert-level napping, enthusiastic ball chasing, professional butt sniffing, and operating a tail that moves at approximately the speed of a helicopter. His favorite workplace activities include chewing on his bone, greeting every visitor who walks through the door, and occasionally forgetting that jumping on people is against company policy.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">As Head of Security, no passing vehicle, pedestrian, or suspicious noise goes unreported. Bruno also enforces a strict company-wide food tax—collected by resting his chin on someone’s lap and deploying his most irresistible puppy-dog eyes. His favorite benefits include fruit, walks, belly rubs, and unlimited opportunities to supervise absolutely nothing.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Beyond his impressive resume, Bruno has one very important job: making people smile. It’s practically impossible to walk into Forged Labor and not have your day brightened by Bruno.</p>
                    <div style="background: #000000; color: var(--brand-accent); padding: 0.6rem 1rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.85rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                        ★ Employee of the Month: Every month. Unanimous decision.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </article>

        </div>

        <!-- =========================================
             MEET OUR MOVING CREW
             ========================================= -->
        <div style="margin-top: 4.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem); color: var(--brand-accent); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); letter-spacing: -0.01em;">
                IN THE FIELD
            </h2>
            <h4 style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: #000000; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 900;">
                MEET OUR MOVING CREW
            </h4>
        </div>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 2rem;">

            <!-- Tobin Jackson -->
            <article class="accordion-box" style="padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <img src="images/team-tobin.jpg" alt="Tobin Jackson - Professional Mover, Forged Labor" style="width: 96px; height: 96px; flex-shrink: 0; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; border: 2px solid #000000;" />
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.4rem; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                            TOBIN JACKSON
                        </h3>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #383838; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">
                            Professional Mover | Forged Labor
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accordion-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Originally from Etowah, Tennessee, Tobin Jackson became part of the Forged Labor family after his brother-in-law, Tee, introduced him to the company. What started as an opportunity to help out on a few moving jobs quickly turned into something much more meaningful. Today, Tobin is an integral part of the crew, bringing dedication, compassion, and a positive attitude to every job.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Outside of work, Tobin enjoys spending quality time with his son and his girl, especially taking trips to the mountains. Whether he’s exploring rivers, enjoying scenic views, or simply spending time outdoors, Tobin has a deep appreciation for nature and the peace it brings. He’s also proud of his biracial heritage and appreciates the different perspectives and experiences that come with it.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">For Tobin, the most rewarding part of working at Forged Labor isn’t simply helping people move—it’s the connections he makes along the way. He believes every customer deserves the same level of care, kindness, and respect, regardless of their circumstances. One experience that particularly touched him involved helping a family move into a beautiful home after the parents had spent 16 years living in an RV. Seeing their happiness reminded him exactly why he loves what he does.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0;">Tobin often says that while the crew helps customers, those customers have just as much of an impact on the people serving them. His promise to every customer is simple: to provide the most efficient moving experience possible while treating their belongings with care, showing genuine kindness, and bringing a friendly smile and a little laughter along the way.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

        </div>

        <!-- Additional Crew Profiles Coming Soon + Booking CTA -->
        <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem; background: #000000; color: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #000000; border-left: 6px solid var(--brand-accent); padding: 2rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem;">
            <div style="max-width: 720px;">
                <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--brand-accent); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; text-transform: uppercase;">
                    MORE CREW PROFILES &amp; PHOTOS ON THE WAY
                </h3>
                <p style="color: #d4d4d8; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
                    We’re continuing to add individual biographies and portraits for the rest of our field movers. Ready to put our crew to work?
                </p>
            </div>
            <a href="/appointments" class="sqsp-btn-pill-yellow">
                BOOK OUR CREW
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

